cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SCM Framework v2.5 — Regime-dependent astrophysical dynamics (SPARC + LITTLE THINGS + MOJAVE)"
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: "2.5.0"

authors:

- family-names: "Cámara Madrid"
  given-names: "Sergio"

identifiers:

- type: doi
  value: "10.5281/zenodo.19455777"

repository-code: "https://github.com/sergiocamaramadrid-cyber/Motor-de-Velos-SCM"

abstract: >-
  The SCM framework validates regime-dependent dynamics across independent
  astrophysical datasets (SPARC galaxies N=100, LITTLE THINGS dwarfs N=26,
  MOJAVE jets N=65). Key results: mass-dependent regime transition in SPARC
  at logMbar < 9.7 (ΔAIC ≈ 8.8, p_perm ≈ 0.043); weak replication in LITTLE
  THINGS; clear transition in MOJAVE jets (r15 ≈ 13.8 pc, bootstrap ≈ 92%).
  This release validates the SCM framework as a regime-detection tool rather
  than a universal law model.

keywords:

- astrophysics
- galaxy dynamics
- SPARC
- LITTLE THINGS
- MOJAVE
- rotation curves
- regime transitions
- reproducibility
